00:33:46.806 --> 00:33:47.972
MELANIE WARRICK: No worries.

00:33:47.972 --> 00:33:51.690
TIMNIT GEBRU: But if you
go to fatconference.org,

00:33:51.690 --> 00:33:54.960
you'll see who the editors are
and who the program chair is

00:33:54.960 --> 00:33:55.930
and things like this.

00:33:55.930 --> 00:33:57.804
MARGARET MITCHELL: Yeah,
so this was actually

00:33:57.804 --> 00:34:02.520
started as a workshop at NIPS,
which is a top deep learning

00:34:02.520 --> 00:34:04.490
conference.

00:34:04.490 --> 00:34:06.780
I believe Solon
Barocas and Moritz

00:34:06.780 --> 00:34:11.489
Hardt were the original sort
of creators a few years back.

00:34:11.489 --> 00:34:16.110
And that was before it
was super hot, super hip

00:34:16.110 --> 00:34:20.580
to look at diversity and policy
and these kinds of issues.

00:34:20.580 --> 00:34:23.080
They were really interested
in combining machine learning

00:34:23.080 --> 00:34:29.310
and law, things like taking
the Civil Rights Act from 1964

00:34:29.310 --> 00:34:31.360
and its notion of
disparate impact

00:34:31.360 --> 00:34:33.000
and then applying
that mathematically

00:34:33.000 --> 00:34:35.639
to something like
demographic parity,

00:34:35.639 --> 00:34:37.260
and so really making
those connections

00:34:37.260 --> 00:34:41.310
between the legal world and
the ML mathematical world.

00:34:41.310 --> 00:34:45.150
And it's really gotten
tons of interest

00:34:45.150 --> 00:34:47.739
and really started making
some strides in this space.

00:34:47.739 --> 00:34:49.920
And so now it's become
its own conference.

00:34:49.920 --> 00:34:56.010
And it switched from FAT/ML
to FAT* as a kind of nod

00:34:56.010 --> 00:34:57.720
to regular expressions.

00:34:57.720 --> 00:35:00.960
So its Fairness, Accountability,
and Transparency, not

00:35:00.960 --> 00:35:03.220
just for machine learning
but for lots of other things

00:35:03.220 --> 00:35:03.790
as well.

00:35:03.790 --> 00:35:04.270
TIMNIT GEBRU: You know what?

00:35:04.270 --> 00:35:05.920
What I'm excited
about this conference

00:35:05.920 --> 00:35:07.810
is the fact that it's
interdisciplinary.

00:35:07.810 --> 00:35:10.930
Again, I am a huge fan of
interdisciplinary teams

00:35:10.930 --> 00:35:11.840
in general.

00:35:11.840 --> 00:35:15.200
And one of the things
that I haven't seen before

00:35:15.200 --> 00:35:17.020
