00:40:00.160 --> 00:40:01.370
MELANIE WARRICK:
It's all on Twitter.

00:40:01.370 --> 00:40:03.250
But you both were
talking about, is there

00:40:03.250 --> 00:40:06.670
a GCP service that handles
Cloud Identity-Aware

00:40:06.670 --> 00:40:10.090
Proxy, especially host
via cloud storage?

00:40:10.090 --> 00:40:11.444
So, Mark, is there?

00:40:11.444 --> 00:40:12.360
MARK MANDEL: Is there?

00:40:12.360 --> 00:40:15.102
OK, so if people aren't aware
of Cloud Identity-Aware Proxy,

00:40:15.102 --> 00:40:17.560
it's a proxy that you can put
in front of your applications

00:40:17.560 --> 00:40:19.150
that controls whether
people have access,

00:40:19.150 --> 00:40:20.890
basically, through
their account logins.

00:40:20.890 --> 00:40:23.050
It works with App Engine
standard, App Engine

00:40:23.050 --> 00:40:25.780
flexible environment, Compute
Engine, and Kubernetes engine.

00:40:25.780 --> 00:40:27.380
But what KF wants
to do is put it

00:40:27.380 --> 00:40:30.040
in front of Google Cloud
Storage for static sides.

00:40:30.040 --> 00:40:33.640
So the short answer
is, unfortunately, no.

00:40:33.640 --> 00:40:36.190
But there are a couple of
interesting workarounds

00:40:36.190 --> 00:40:38.680
that I think are
worth discussing.

00:40:38.680 --> 00:40:41.260
The first one is, and it's
a bit of a cheeky answer,

00:40:41.260 --> 00:40:44.410
but you can always host static
content on App Engine itself.

00:40:44.410 --> 00:40:45.654
There's no reason why not.

00:40:45.654 --> 00:40:47.320
It's actually really,
really easy to do.

00:40:47.320 --> 00:40:48.310
There's a lot of
opportunities there

00:40:48.310 --> 00:40:49.520
for putting static content.

00:40:49.520 --> 00:40:51.370
And if you're using some
sort of programming language

00:40:51.370 --> 00:40:52.480
and you wanted to mix
and match, there's

00:40:52.480 --> 00:40:54.580
also opportunities to do
stuff like that as well.

00:40:54.580 --> 00:40:55.700
So that's always a thing.

00:40:55.700 --> 00:40:57.100
So you could always
put the static content,

00:40:57.100 --> 00:40:58.580
rather than putting it
in Google Cloud Storage,

00:40:58.580 --> 00:41:00.760
you can put it on App Engine and
then put Cloud Identity-Aware

00:41:00.760 --> 00:41:02.140
Proxy in front of
that, and you still

00:41:02.140 --> 00:41:03.780
get a lot of the really
great edge caching you would

00:41:03.780 --> 00:41:04.960
get on Google Cloud Storage.

00:41:04.960 --> 00:41:07.989
The other option is
a open-source product

00:41:07.989 --> 00:41:09.530
that's available on
GitHub, and we'll

00:41:09.530 --> 00:41:10.750
have the links in
the show notes.

00:41:10.750 --> 00:41:12.750
It's called Weasel, which
is an interesting name

00:41:12.750 --> 00:41:14.950
in and of itself, which
is basically an App Engine

00:41:14.950 --> 00:41:18.020
proxy for basically files
that you store on Google Cloud

00:41:18.020 --> 00:41:18.940
Storage.

00:41:18.940 --> 00:41:20.964
So you could put this
up on App Engine,

00:41:20.964 --> 00:41:23.130
then just change whatever
you need to change or host

00:41:23.130 --> 00:41:25.379
whatever you need to host
inside Google Cloud Storage,

00:41:25.379 --> 00:41:28.420
and then put the Identity-Aware
Proxy in front of that data

00:41:28.420 --> 00:41:29.260
application that
runs on App Engine.

00:41:29.260 --> 00:41:29.920
MELANIE WARRICK: And
it's called Weasel?

00:41:29.920 --> 00:41:31.253
MARK MANDEL: It's called Weasel.

00:41:31.253 --> 00:41:31.900
Yeah, I--

